{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers","id":807377,"title":"Open Dev Three: Slash! Slash! Slashers!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T15:54:41-08:00","id":807377,"title":"Open Dev Three: Slash! Slash! Slashers!","content":"It's up!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slash-slash-slashers/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-ope...lash-slashers/</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My thoughts:<br /> <br /> Perhaps it will be an unpopular opinion, but I'm somewhat wary of creating a prominent connection between Slashers and fallen Hunters. A story of a Hunter gone bad can be very powerful and I think putting Slashers at the forefront can distract from all other ways it could happen.<br /> <br /> The Vigil is a very stressful undertaking and I can easily see Hunters become extremists, use their resources for selfish purposes, create criminal enterprises, lash out at their close ones, grow resentful of people who do not protect themselves, be broken by the hard decisions they've taken, sell out to Monsters or Conspiracies. I'm afraid that overly focusing on the Slashers can give an impression that this kind of failure is all there is. It can be easily avoided by careful writing.<br /> <br /> Also, it would bear explaining why a Hunter suddenly shifts their quarry towards ordinary Humans. There is a difference between growing callous and outright taking up serial murder. Of course, a Slasher could choose targets valid for the Vigil, but it doesn't carry the same visceral feelings as a human monster stalking the innocent. Additionally, I am curious of the difference between Slashers and ordinary serial killers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":".  Added text. 01-12-2016, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:55:25-08:00","id":807379,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slash-slash-slashers/\" target=\"_blank\">New open dev!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:06:59-08:00","id":807392,"title":"","content":"Getting into some nice meat and gristle now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:46:24-08:00","id":807420,"title":"","content":"1) Slashers are based on a prevalent horror trope that often generates a lot of complex feelings. If you had to come up with a definition of a slasher that you know you and your group would be happy with, what would it be?<br /> <br /> My group generally sees Slashers as the dark counterpart of Hunters, a humbling reminder of what they could end up as, if they aren't careful about the way they uphold the Vigil.<br /> <br /> 2) Does the possibility of becoming a slasher sound interesting to you? Why or why not?<br /> <br /> Only as a cautionary tale. &quot;If you keep going down that road, you'll go Slasher.&quot; Basically, the idea that if you go too far off the deep end, you'll end up as an NPC. Playable slashers? Not my thing.<br /> <br /> 3) Could you see yourself using a slasher cabal in your game? If so, how?<br /> <br /> Only rarely. Slashers are usually solitary creatures.<br /> <br /> 4) If you said \u201cyes,\u201d to Question 2, would you want the rules to support your transformation from hunter-to-slasher? Or, would you prefer this be kept more vague?<br /> <br /> Vague. More or less a guideline of things hunters avoid doing due to the risk of becoming Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:51:14-08:00","id":807425,"title":"","content":"This looks like it's going in an excellent direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:43:10-08:00","id":807455,"title":"","content":"Reposted from the comments on the Blog:<br /> <br /> 1.) A Slasher is a monster, often (but not always) a serial killer, who used to be human. Michael Meyers, Jason Voorhees, Freddie Kruger, Pinhead, The Tall Man, Chucky... They were all human at one point, but at the time the films that star them take place, they're all distinctly supernatural in one way or another. On the other hand, Norman Bates, Leatherface, Hannibal Lecter, the various killers behind the Ghostface, Jigsaw? They're &quot;just&quot; human serial killers, monstrous but not actual monsters. By the same token, the Leprechaun from Leprechaun, the Djinn from Wishmaster, the monster from Jeepers Creepers, they're all &quot;just&quot; monsters with a pattern to the way they kill people. To me, a slasher needs both to have been human, and then to have crossed the line that separates human from monsters. <br /> <br /> 2.) Absolutely. To me, Hunter the Vigil is all about characters who straddle the line between human and monster - both figuratively in the &quot;monstrous behavior&quot; sense, and literally, in the sense that some Hunters use actual supernatural powers. To me, Slashers are the natural outcome of Hunters who go too far, and the personal horror of Hunter comes in questioning just where that line actually is.<br /> <br /> 3.) Eh, Cabals of Slashers don't really interest me that much.<br /> <br /> 4.) I agree with some of the other comments saying that the distinction between Hunter and Slasher should be subtle enough that the character is constantly asking themselves if they might be a Slasher. On the other hand, you should be able to easily recognize a Slasher when you see one. There's this incredibly powerful moment in Bloodborne when you first encounter Father Gascoigne. He's brutally hacking away at an obviously dead Beast, but as you approach he turns his attention to you and mumbles &quot;Beasts all over the shop... You'll be one of them... Sooner or later...&quot; In that one 30 second or so cutscene, I instantly understood that every Hunter was just a hair's breadth away from being one of the Beasts they hunt, and that Father Gascoigne had crossed that line. He was killing indiscriminately, and using &quot;they'll all be Beasts eventually&quot; as an excuse, and I had to kill him before he did the same to me. I also wondered, &quot;how long until I end up like that?&quot; and a little part of me wondered if I already was like that. After all, I was trying to kill him with the same justification he was using to try to kill me. If the 2e rules for Hunters becoming Slashers can allow for moments like that, I will consider it a tremendous success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:52:22-08:00","id":807465,"title":"","content":"To me, the question of how a hunter becomes a slasher is linked to the question of what 2e should do with the Code. Here's how I'd do it: <br /> <br /> 2e should have a version of the Code that inoculates the hunter from Breaking Points at the cost of picking up a Tell (modeled by a Persistent Condition), with guidelines as to how this differs from a more natural evolution of the hunter's Breaking Points. To become a Slasher (more specifically, a Ripper), two things must happen: the hunter must choose to use the Code to negate killing as a Breaking Point; and the Hunter must adopt a murder-based Aspiration. Once these two conditions are met, the hunter becomes a Ripper and is eligible to pick up an Undertaking. You don't need an Undertaking to be a Ripper, and a Ripper who doesn't have an Undertaking differs from a hunter only psychologically. <br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> need an Undertaking to become a Scourge, though; to become a scourge, the slasher must transition from a Ripper Undertaking to the associated Scourge Undertaking. I'm not sure yet what the requirements for that would be; possibly just an appropriate expenditure of Practical Experience. Once you become a scourge, you enter Monster territory: you gain a dot of Potency and can develop Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T23:33:58-08:00","id":807651,"title":"","content":"Huh, I have to say that the blog post made me wonder somewhat, it made some assumptions that makes the difference between monster and nonmonster less blurry than it has been.<br /> <br /> 1) You have to be a monster to have dread powers, which certainly wasn't the case in hunter first edition, since hunters could take dread powers as endowments, with ST permission of course, and even cultists could sport some dread powers. <br /> <br /> 2) That monsters can't have integrity, which isn't what mortal remains says, it says monsters can have alternate breaking points, not that they have to. <br /> <br /> Me, I like the blurriness, I'd have developing a dread power not a good sign, but then again the lucifuge aren't all slashers, so maybe it's not the end of the world, etc. <br /> <br /> I'd rather have guidelines not a checklist.<br /> <br /> As for keeping endowments, that would really depend on the endowment. Maybe a cainite slasher stops getting vials of blood in the mail, and Valkyrie switches your chip off when they realize you went off the reservation, but I doubt a lucifuge's demonic blood requires a morality test, or that an AO just magically forgets all their recipes, and Aegis will want their relics back, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:18:15-08:00","id":807675,"title":"","content":"reposting from the blog<br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1) the short answer- human monsters. The long answer- people who has lost their humanity while pursuing an obsession, turning mad in the process and unlocking dread abilities which flows from the cracks in their broken soul. People who have a twisted way to look in the world which distance them from it, and which justifies their killings. People who are no longer people, simply because they lack empathy, passion and the ability to recognize that what they are doing is wrong. Again, human monsters.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2)I don\u2019t think I feel comfortable with playing a character (or allowing to play a character) which is a slasher or slasher in the becoming simply because the idea of slashers makes me feel uncomfortable. While using them as antagonists is ok, just the thought about them as PCs creeps me out- which is why I think there must be rules for how an hunter may turn into a slasher. Showing people the possibility how their character may fall into that dark state and maybe even playing with it along until reaching that boundary should, without doubt, be a feature of the Slasher Chronicles, because this is an horror game and if it makes me scared it should be the right path, and it could also makes some great stories!</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also, hunters need to have Touchstones, and losing them should be a part of the path into \u201cslasherhood\u201d.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3)ammm is it ok to say that, in many ways, I\u2019m already using such Cabals? I mean, yeah, I didn\u2019t called them Cabals (I used the term \u201cSlashing Compacts/Conspiracies\u201d, but I already have a number of big organizations based around killing and justifying their killing- some also hunt monsters, others focus on killing other people, but all in all groups murdering innocent people for faith, discovery, lust for power and even hope for a brighter future all took and take a part in my games, both as antagonists and protagonists. Having that possibility fully supported in the new Core Hunter is something I would like to see.</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T01:32:39-08:00","id":807709,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m all in for the hunters-to-slasher transformation and I totally approve idea for the 2ED corebook. Now to the questions\u2026<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If you had to come up with a definition of a slasher that you know you and your group would be happy with, what would it be?</li> </ol>Serial killer that need to fulfil his urge to kill, in the specific way. His urges can heighten with each kill and Modus Operand sophisticate, but base idea is all from the beginning. If he was hunter before, he probably see humans the same way as monsters, not seeing any difference between hunting one and another. I want slashers to be able to be played like Dexter character from the TV series \u2013 he has his urges to kill, but can, in the end, be rather stable \u2013 IF he will kill people.<br /> I\u2019m also for the return of Undertakings for the slashers, if there is possibility of it.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does the possibility of becoming a slasher sound interesting to you? Why or why not?</li> </ol><br /> I think it\u2019s very interesting possibility. In our Hunter game I play hunter that more and more goes in to darkness of violence \u2013 I do not think I would want the character to be truly consumed by it, yet, but I would very likely easily could see the moment of slipping in to is near. It\u2019s thrilling experience, and I would very much look for it.<br /> <br /> 3) Could you see yourself using a slasher cabal in your game? If so, how?<br /> <br /> If I would be a ST, I would probably made slasher cabal as major chronicle antagonist, \u201cenemy within\u201d style. If possibility of hunters become the slashers was in rules, I would made \u201calmost there\u201d group of hunters between various cells, Compacts and Conspiracies be connected over one dark matter from their past ( maybe one hunting went very bad ) to drag them all over the boundary. New cabal would start as cleaning the mess that started it, but probably become more and more self-obsessed with each other killing urges. Still, they could coordinate they attacks if their secret would be put to danger. They would be secret cancer cell in the many cells structure.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would you want the rules to support your transformation from hunter-to-slasher? Or, would you prefer this be kept more vague?</li> </ol>I would want the rules to support transformation. I would went rather with Condition and Aspiration way of \u201cslasher to be\u201d \u2013 in that solution character could be changed more gently. And also your character to be saved if the process is interrupted \u2013 or character changed it ways. But I think on the end of it, new slasher should get some Dread Powers \u2013 maybe as Undertakings? Going down all the way to Integrity 0 would mean that all slashers are half catatonic maniacs that can\u2019t pull themselves together \u2013 and it is a bad way to do it. Dexter-like characters should be most prevailing slashers \u2013 few really demented ones ( with Integrity 0 ) could be possible \u2013 but most should be resistant from total insanity. More and more extensive Tells list could also nicely add up to the Modus Operandi development, with each Tell marking character more and more in to slasher territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T01:50:20-08:00","id":807715,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't put any direct Integrity requirement on becoming a Slasher \u2014 that worked for Morality because, well, it was Morality; but Integrity is about how damaged your soul is, and while a Slasher probably took some hits in that regard on his way to becoming what he is, a badly damaged soul is not strictly necessary. What's necessary is the urge to kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:13:30-08:00","id":807789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers#post807377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vigil is a very stressful undertaking and I can easily see Hunters become extremists, use their resources for selfish purposes, create criminal enterprises, lash out at their close ones, grow resentful of people who do not protect themselves, be broken by the hard decisions they've taken, sell out to Monsters or Conspiracies. I'm afraid that overly focusing on the Slashers can give an impression that this kind of failure is all there is. It can be easily avoided by careful writing.<br /> <br /> Also, it would bear explaining why a Hunter suddenly shifts their quarry towards ordinary Humans. There is a difference between growing callous and outright taking up serial murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own reasoning on this, reposted from the blog comments is:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">I don\u2019t have an interest in going from *hunter* to slasher (*human* to slasher maybe). To me a hunter going bad means ever more zeal for monsters: disregard for collateral damage, and eager killing of perceived minions and associates, sure; but also an increasing disregard for whether particular monsters are dangerous or innocent.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">But slashers *focus* on humans. It doesn\u2019t make a lot of sense for a hunter who goes off the rails to switch focus to humans over monsters \u2013 and having slashers see their victims as adjuncts to monsters narrows their range too much.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">And if hunters going bad become slashers, and thus focus on humans over monsters, this lets one of Hunter\u2019s biggest moral questions \u2013 that of whether killing supernaturals (or *this* supernatural) is right \u2013 off the hook.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">So if slashers are to be a dark mirror to hunters, I think it should be the parallel of their actions \u2013 that they stalk and kill, and are hunters better just because they focus on a more socially acceptable target (hell, many slashers focus on targets that society tacitly accepts even if it pretends otherwise) \u2013 that\u2019s at the root of it.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:57:58-08:00","id":807841,"title":"","content":"Just got epiphany how Hunter's Code and becoming Slasher should work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>If we treat Tells as special Conditions you take instead of Breaking Point, then <i>character become Slasher when she has &lt;Integrity&gt; numbers of Tells and become Ripper</i></b> - that means the stable character ( like Integrity 7 starting ) will need a large number of Tells ( 7 in this example ). And character that is unstable ( Integrity 1-2 ) only a small traumatic push with Tells ( with number of 1 or 2 ). And yes, becoming Soul Less <b><i>could</i></b> easily turn you in Slasher - but is not sure in this way ( you need Tell in the first place ).<br /> <br /> <b>Notice:</b> I do not know if Integrity 0 character is a thing, but even then we could limit to at least 1 Tell needed to Slasher transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-13-2016, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:10:50-08:00","id":807940,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">1) Slashers are inhuman humans, monsters for what they do rather than what they are. They can't relate to humanity at large anymore, don't understand right from wrong, are compelled to kill, divorced from reality, or lacking all empathy. Eventually they aren't human anymore - they're dead souled monsters drawing power from the evil that they do.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2) Hunters becoming Slashers underlines the theme of human frailty and the question of what it means to be human. From a play point of view I think it gives people a chance to ape stories of people who have been pushed past the point of burnout or becoming what they fought against. It provides a terrible psychological consequence to character's choosing expedience or violence to solve moral dilemmas.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3) Cabals of Slashers would be a nice way to model a 'mirror' foe without Hunters having to kill other Hunters. For a Storyteller it would give a means to make Slashers more than just a singular monster of the week antagonist. I would probably use them as either a direct analog to the Hunter's Cell - there but for the grace of God sort of thing - or a well connected network that lets its members get away with all manner of horror, like say the Court of Owls from Batman or 'the family' from True Detective. Although, now I'm picturing a Hills Have Eyes cannibal fest and that seems pretty cool too.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4) Clear rules to support transformation from a Hunter to Slasher would give players and Storytellers the guidelines to not have to hand wave when a character makes the leap from one to the other. I think maybe tying it to the Integrity system in a way that lets you alter your character's answers to the Integrity questions might be a way to make it work. This is the approach I've taken in my God Machine Chronicle rules Hunter the Vigil game. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:27:37-08:00","id":807950,"title":"","content":"<b>Question 1: Definition of Slasher</b><br /> <br /> First of all I'd define a Slasher as <u>an antagonist designed to mechanically replicate the tropes associated with the vilians of the Slasher Movie genera.</u> Not any serial killer qualifies, not even every slightly supernatural serial killer qualifies. An Apostle of the Dark One (Second Sight Thamaturge) who regularly commits human sacrifice is unlikely to be a Slasher.<br /> <br /> To give a more solid definition, I'd say the following four traits are key<br /> <br /> 1. They're a serial killer who primarally targets regular mortals.<br /> <br /> 2. They fall on a power level ranging from non-supernatural but inhumanly skilled (think Jigsaw) to low powered supernatural: Freddy Kruger is undeniably using supernatural abilities but he's only got a few tricks and I would say that a Mage or Changeling could easily outdo him at dream manipulation.<br /> <br /> 3. They have an exceptionally strong sense of theme that they're psychologically or supernaturally compelled to follow. Iconic outfits, a persistent modus operandi, favoured weapons. Etc<br /> <br /> 4. A Slasher's psychological issues form the core of their charachter and are the source of their borderline-supernatural or outright-supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Question 2: Am I interested in the possibility of my hunter becoming a Slasher</b><br /> <br /> Not in particular. My Hunter charachters have never focused that strongly on killing monsters, and while I am interested in the potential for them to fall it never felt right that they'd become Slashers if they hit the bottom. For example I once played a Task Force: VALKARIE signal intelligence officer. I could see him becoming possessed by some strange entity that lives in the wires, or becoming a Mage after he gets an Obsession with some strange signal he detects. But a Slasher just doesn\u2019t fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> To me Slashers were always a Dark Mirror to Hunters. They have similar obessive personalities. Like Hunters their primary goals involve killing (Excluding Null Mysteriis, Network Zero, etc).<br /> <br /> What made them interesting was not the risk of becoming a Slasher, but how Hunters justified why they were different from Slashers. The Hunter says &quot;I kill vampires&quot;, the Slasher says &quot;I kill sinners&quot;. Is the Hunter morally better? The answer is yes, but explaining why is a rich and interesting source of character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Question 3: Could you see yourself using a slasher cabal in your game.</b><br /> <br /> Not at all. To me every single interesting thing about Slashers traces back to the same root: The Slasher's psychology. The moment you stop thinking of the Slasher and start thinking of the Cabal you distance the story from the Slasher's psychology.<br /> <br /> To illustrate this, The Hunt Club doesn't have a single mention of Undertakings in it's write up, and their focus on pleasing judges who's tastes change makes it nearly impossible to have the hyper focused Modeus Operandi that Slashers are known for.<br /> <br /> I like the Hunt Club, but I wouldn't actually call them Slashers. A question to the audience, which 1E Undertakings do you feel would work for members of the Hunt Club, and why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers#post807377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it will be an unpopular opinion, but I'm somewhat wary of creating a prominent connection between Slashers and fallen Hunters. A story of a Hunter gone bad can be very powerful and I think putting Slashers at the forefront can distract from all other ways it could happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same waryness. I'm also wary that creating too much of a connection would dilute what made the 1E Slashers such focused and effective villains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=807465#post807465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e should have a version of the Code that inoculates the hunter from Breaking Points at the cost of picking up a Tell (modeled by a Persistent Condition), with guidelines as to how this differs from a more natural evolution of the hunter's Breaking Points. To become a Slasher (more specifically, a Ripper), two things must happen: the hunter must choose to use the Code to negate killing as a Breaking Point; and the Hunter must adopt a murder-based Aspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'd do it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpanishInquisition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=807940#post807940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t have an interest in going from *hunter* to slasher (*human* to slasher maybe). To me a hunter going bad means ever more zeal for monsters: disregard for collateral damage, and eager killing of perceived minions and associates, sure; but also an increasing disregard for whether particular monsters are dangerous or innocent.<br /> <br /> But slashers *focus* on humans. It doesn\u2019t make a lot of sense for a hunter who goes off the rails to switch focus to humans over monsters \u2013 and having slashers see their victims as adjuncts to monsters narrows their range too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed in all counts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:35:47-08:00","id":807959,"title":"","content":"I think restricting Slashers to the narrow slasher trope is not only a waste of material but a dilution of theme (as slasher movies are often campy and unserious, and can dilute the theme of a more serious chronicle). I've actually never run a Slasher as the &quot;slasher movie villain.&quot; Not even once. All my Slashers have been people who have become defined by the act of murder, one way or another, and their current existence revolves around killing.<br /> <br /> I would agree with the psychological angle, but then again, what intelligent being <i>doesn't</i> have psychological issues? The reason psychological issues are so revealing/damning in the case of Slashers is because their single-minded focus on a single activity opens them up to have clear strengths and weaknesses. The same could be said of any person that devotes themselves to a single activity. Eventually your psychological issues will come to the fore, and you will become easier to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:45:09-08:00","id":807965,"title":"","content":"A relevant bit of text from <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>'s rules update appendix that I can't find in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>\u201cMy Character Kills People All the Time\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Is it possible for a character to reach a point where killing another human being is not a breaking point? Players might make the argument for soldiers, policemen, gang members or good-hearted serial killers to be exempt from suffering breaking points from taking a life, up to a point. For mortal, non-supernatural characters, our recommendation is that if a character kills a person, it's always a breaking point, even if the player gets a positive modifier to the roll. <br /> <br /> Note that we said \u201cmortal, non-supernatural\u201d character. Vampires, werewolves and other shadow-folk aren't fully human and don't play by the same rules. Their rules, in fact, will be addressed in the appropriate books.</span></div><br /> This blurb was my inspiration for saying that removing the Breaking Point for murder is a key part of becoming a Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-13-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:47:01-08:00","id":807969,"title":"","content":"I love your definition of a Slasher, TKR!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T09:59:12-08:00","id":807975,"title":"","content":"Why thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:09:16-08:00","id":807984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=807465#post807465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, the question of how a hunter becomes a slasher is linked to the question of what 2e should do with the Code. Here's how I'd do it: <br /> <br /> 2e should have a version of the Code that inoculates the hunter from Breaking Points at the cost of picking up a Tell (modeled by a Persistent Condition), with guidelines as to how this differs from a more natural evolution of the hunter's Breaking Points. To become a Slasher (more specifically, a Ripper), two things must happen: the hunter must choose to use the Code to negate killing as a Breaking Point; and the Hunter must adopt a murder-based Aspiration. Once these two conditions are met, the hunter becomes a Ripper and is eligible to pick up an Undertaking. You don't need an Undertaking to be a Ripper, and a Ripper who doesn't have an Undertaking differs from a hunter only psychologically.<br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> need an Undertaking to become a Scourge, though; to become a scourge, the slasher must transition from a Ripper Undertaking to the associated Scourge Undertaking. I'm not sure yet what the requirements for that would be; possibly just an appropriate expenditure of Practical Experience. Once you become a scourge, you enter Monster territory: you gain a dot of Potency and can develop Dread Powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an absolutely great way to handle the transition, because each step makes sense as something a Hunter might do, and they present a logical path for the well-intentioned extremist to become a character defined by murder. Removing killing as a Breaking Point seems like a logical choice for any Hunter, because they kill a *lot* of sentient monsters. And the second requirement makes it easy to justify because you can always tell yourself &quot;it's fine as long as I don't take an Aspiration to kill anyone&quot;. But when that one target eludes you time after time, and you start getting more and more obsessed with taking it down...<br /> <br /> What ever system they end up using, I hope it creates as smooth and natural a path to Slasherdom as this suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:16:39-08:00","id":807994,"title":"","content":"I like the concept but I would specify that the Code must nullify murdering <u>mortals</u> as a Breaking Point and then you need an Aspiration to kill a mortal. The classic, &quot;Monsters Don't Count&quot; is not enough.<br /> <br /> Otherwise monster-of-the-week themed games where a vampire dies every session would be either unplayable (or at least unthematic) due to plummeting Integrity or everyone turning into a Slasher the moment they put stakeing a vampire down as an Aspiration. Dean and Sam's Integrity plummeted, but it wasn't guilt from slaying vampire's that did it.<br /> <br /> If you specify mortals you still have an incentive to take the Code - it's hard to fight a vampire when you have to keep his human minions alive. And once that police detective (Dominated? Just suspicious that a crate of explosives went missing?) causes a bit too much trouble for your Cell... I think specifying mortals is a better balance that still presents a silky smooth Hunter-&gt;Slasher transition, without making common playstyles unworkable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Taking the Code and avoiding taking the Aspiration to kill any monsters sounds a bit too meta-gaming for my taste. I would say that if you spend more than a few in-charachter hours planning to kill a monster it probably should be an Aspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:02:26-08:00","id":808049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=807994#post807994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the concept but I would specify that the Code must nullify murdering <u>mortals</u> as a Breaking Point and then you need an Aspiration to kill a mortal. The classic, &quot;Monsters Don't Count&quot; is not enough.<br /> <br /> Otherwise monster-of-the-week themed games where a vampire dies every session would be either unplayable (or at least unthematic) due to plummeting Integrity or everyone turning into a Slasher the moment they put stakeing a vampire down as an Aspiration. Dean and Sam's Integrity plummeted, but it wasn't guilt from slaying vampire's that did it.<br /> <br /> If you specify mortals you still have an incentive to take the Code - it's hard to fight a vampire when you have to keep his human minions alive. And once that police detective (Dominated? Just suspicious that a crate of explosives went missing?) causes a bit too much trouble for your Cell... I think specifying mortals is a better balance that still presents a silky smooth Hunter-&gt;Slasher transition, without making common playstyles unworkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Killing a vampire should be a Breaking Point the same way killing a human is, that's why they need the Code in the first place. That's part of the personal horror of Hunter, is that you're playing characters that regularly kill intelligent creatures, and one way or another, that takes its toll on your psyche. If you don't want to risk becoming a Slasher, you've got to get clever. Remove killing *vampires* as a Breaking Point if you hunt a lot of vampires. Or, alternatively, spend experience to keep your Integrity up. Or just accept the fact that people who hunt monsters end up with a lot of Conditions. At least those conditions are a good source of Beats to buy your lost Integrity back with. But if you take the easy route and remove killing *in general* as a Breaking Point, you're on your way to becoming a monster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=807994#post807994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the Code and avoiding taking the Aspiration to kill any monsters sounds a bit too meta-gaming for my taste. I would say that if you spend more than a few in-charachter hours planning to kill a monster it probably should be an Aspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care about metagaming, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:13:54-08:00","id":808063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808049#post808049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Killing a vampire should be a Breaking Point the same way killing a human is, that's why they need the Code in the first place. That's part of the personal horror of Hunter, is that you're playing characters that regularly kill intelligent creatures, and one way or another, that takes its toll on your psyche.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not everybody plays hunter as personal horror, some play it more as an action/drama game along the lines of Buffy: the Vampire Slayer. While I don't think Hunter needs to go out of it's way to support that playstyle, I think it should avoid mechanically invalidating it.<br /> <br /> If a monster hunter themed toolbox doesn't let you play Buffy, it's not much of a toolbox.<br /> <br /> (For reference, Buffy's kill count: 133 vamps, 62 demons, 6 monsters, 11 humans, 1 spirit warrior &amp; a robot- so this gives Buffy 215 kills in all - thanks IMDB)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808049#post808049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remove killing *vampires* as a Breaking Point if you hunt a lot of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you drawing the line between &quot;Vampires&quot; and &quot;All Monsters&quot;, instead of between &quot;All Monsters&quot; and &quot;Anyone&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:32:53-08:00","id":808084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808063#post808063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not everybody plays hunter as personal horror, some play it more as an action/drama game along the lines of Buffy: the Vampire Slayer. While I don't think Hunter needs to go out of it's way to support that playstyle, I think it should avoid mechanically invalidating it.<br /> <br /> If a monster hunter themed toolbox doesn't let you play Buffy, it's not much of a toolbox.<br /> <br /> (For reference, Buffy's kill count: 133 vamps, 62 demons, 6 monsters, 11 humans, 1 spirit warrior &amp; a robot- so this gives Buffy 215 kills in all - thanks IMDB)</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal horror is what CofD is all about, in my opinion. The inability to play a game of murderhobos is what separates Hunter from D20 Modern featuring lots of vampires and werewolves. I just don't think it's the right system for playing Buffy, at least not by default. It's a great system for <i>deconstructing</i> Buffy, but if you want to play Buffy straight, you're going to need some optional rules and system hacks. And I've got no issue with optional rules and system hacks, but I do think that in order to keep Hunter in-theme with the rest of CofD, you shouldn't be able to kill any thinking beings without psychological consequences by default. Whether those consequences be losing Integrity or turning into a monster is where you can get into the real meat of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808063#post808063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you drawing the line between &quot;Vampires&quot; and &quot;All Monsters&quot;, instead of between &quot;All Monsters&quot; and &quot;Anyone&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because &quot;vampire&quot; has a clear definition. &quot;Monster&quot; does not. That's the core question of Hunter in my opinion, is what defines a monster? A Hunter answers that question for himself when he decides what things it's ok for him to kill. If what he decides is &quot;anything I personally don't recognize as human&quot;, he's putting himself at risk of fitting under someone else's definition of a monster. What happens when he kills something that another Hunter <i>does</i> personally recognize as human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-13-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:37:01-08:00","id":808087,"title":"","content":"As a note, just because people don't play Hunter as personal horror doesn't mean the people writing and designing for it are off the hitch.<br /> <br /> Personal Horror is a central design conceit for ChroD. If you're going to contirbute to these games, you have to contribute with that in mind, because the writers <i>are</i> going to write from that angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:43:04-08:00","id":808095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808084#post808084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I do think that in order to keep Hunter in-theme with the rest of CofD, you shouldn't be able to kill any thinking beings without psychological consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div> Psychological consequences are great, but in the real world soldiers don't have a direct correlation between psychological consequences and number of foreign soldiers they kill.<br /> <br /> Just like Buffy in fact. She did have plenty of psycholgoical consiqunces from her Vigil, she just didn't have a Breaking Point for every last vampire. That is what I would expect a Hunter with a Code to look like, casual about killing monsters. Seriously torn up if a friend gets hurt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808084#post808084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when he kills something that another Hunter <i>does</i> personally recognize as human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those sorts of situations are precisely the reason I like the idea of Hunters saying &quot;monster's don't count&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides, vampires, werewolves, etc don't have clear definitions either. Is a Wolf-Blooded with a Tell that lets them Shapeshift into a wolf a Werwolf? What about a Mage who frequently uses Life to turn into a Wolf and uses the moon as a Yantra?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808087#post808087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, just because people don't play Hunter as personal horror doesn't mean the people writing and designing for it are off the hitch.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fortunately I think it's not only possible but easy to have both<br /> <br /> 1) Personal horror<br /> 2) Not mechanically impossible to play Buffy (as I said in post #21 that's really all I'm asking for here.)<br /> <br /> At the same time.<br /> <br /> After all, 1E did it just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:47:09-08:00","id":808098,"title":"","content":"FWIW, I was thinking of Unknown Armies' rules for callousness when I brought up the 2e version of the Code. It's supposed to be a two-edged thing where you trade one set of problems for another set. That's why I specified Tells as part of it.<br /> <br /> When I suggested that removing killing as a Breaking Point should be the gateway to Slasherhood, I meant killing people. And I'm using \u201cpeople\u201drather than \u201chumans\u201d deliberately, due to the vagueness of the word \u2014 and thus giving the Storyteller some leeway in how to interpret it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:53:08-08:00","id":808106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately I think it's not only possible but easy to have both</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, saying &quot;Not everyone plays Hunter as personal horror&quot; is a useless argument, because even if some people don't ,the writers will write for that angle regardless.<br /> <br /> + mentalities rather than -mentalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:58:08-08:00","id":808112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808098#post808098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, I was thinking of Unknown Armies' rules for callousness when I brought up the 2e version of the Code. It's supposed to be a two-edged thing where you trade one set of problems for another set. That's why I specified Tells as part of it.<br /> <br /> When I suggested that removing killing as a Breaking Point should be the gateway to Slasherhood, I meant killing people. And I'm using \u201cpeople\u201drather than \u201chumans\u201d deliberately, due to the vagueness of the word \u2014 and thus giving the Storyteller some leeway in how to interpret it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like a refluffed Atrocity Dice (from VtR: Danse Macabre) has always felt like a great fit for Hunter.<br /> <br /> Are you hunting to keep people safe, or are you hunting because you really like hurting monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:59:19-08:00","id":808113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like Buffy in fact. She did have plenty of psycholgoical consiqunces from her Vigil, she just didn't have a Breaking Point for every last vampire. That is what I would expect a Hunter with a Code to look like, casual about killing monsters. Seriously torn up if a friend gets hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing inteligent being is Breaking Point. If Buffy do not want to get her Breaking Points from killing vampires and demons - she just take <b>Tell ( Killing vampires )</b> and <b>Tell ( Killing demons )</b>, problem solved.<br /> <br /> She only have a problem if her Integrity comes at 2 or lower - but I do not see it, as she has very high Integrity in rather all the series. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is <i>exactly</i> why I proposed basing &quot;slasher barrier&quot; on Tells-to-Integrity ratio. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's still a totally different situation than &quot;Monsters Do Not Count&quot; <b>Mortal Remains</b> try to sell - paraphrasing last spoiler on Iron in <b>Changeling</b> 2ED:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If it looks like human, sounds like human and quacks as human - it is human.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Or at least should be for your Integrity Breaking Points. You can got small bonuses as for &quot;it's monster and doing bad things&quot;. But in the long way, just use your Tells to make small exceptions individual for your character here and make here do not roll Breaking Point all together.<br /> <br /> That's a small price, that a little step to Slashdom, doesn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-13-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:03:53-08:00","id":808119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Psychological consequences are great, but in the real world soldiers don't have a direct correlation between psychological consequences and number of foreign soldiers they kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the limitations of an abstract rules system. It will never model reality perfectly. In real life, there is a correlation between killing people and having psychological issues. Probably not causation, but definitely correlation. RPG rules are not great at modeling correlation without causation. But they do their best - after all, not every Breaking Point leads to Integrity loss. In fact, not every Breaking Point even leads to a Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like Buffy in fact. She did have plenty of psycholgoical consiqunces from her Vigil, she just didn't have a Breaking Point for every last vampire. That is what I would expect a Hunter with a Code to look like, casual about killing monsters. Seriously torn up if a friend gets hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you could read her as having a tremendous success rate on all those Breaking Point rolls she made. Likely due to all of those Touchstones she had. And when her Touchstones got hurt or killed, then she failed rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those sorts of situations are precisely the reason I like the idea of Hunters saying &amp;quot;monster's don't count&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree entirely. They're also the reason I like the idea that no matter how much Hunters tell themselves &quot;monsters don't count&quot;, monsters totally still count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, vampires, werewolves, etc don't have clear definitions either. Is a Wolf-Blooded with a Tell that lets them Shapeshift into a wolf a Werwolf? What about a Mage who frequently uses Life to turn into a Wolf and uses the moon as a Yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>More reasons I prefer specific types of creatures as exemptions from the Code, rather than monsters in general. The moral ambiguity is what makes it interesting. Who is it or isn't it ok to kill, and what are the moral implications of the lines a character chooses to draw?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808095#post808095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately I think it's not only possible but easy to have both<br /> <br /> 1) Personal horror<br /> 2) Not mechanically impossible to play Buffy<br /> <br /> At the same time.<br /> <br /> After all, 1E did it just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e was fine. I would like 2e to be great. If the writers and developers ever have to make a choice between making the personal horror more compelling, or making other play styles easier to accomodate, I dearly hope they chose the former. This is one case where I think the core themes of the game would be weakened by choosing the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:43:13-08:00","id":808144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808119#post808119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e was fine. I would like 2e to be great. If the writers and developers ever have to make a choice between making the personal horror more compelling, or making other play styles easier to accomodate, I dearly hope they chose the former. This is one case where I think the core themes of the game would be weakened by choosing the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with the principal. However I don't think it would weaken the focus on horror to allow Codes which permit all monsters. In fact, I think it would strengthen the personal horror. Hear me out on this one.<br /> <br /> I think that in most games of hunter (not Network Zero, but definately VALKYRIE) you're supposed to kill monsters regularly. I think that in practice a Breaking Point every time you kill a monster will numb the players and the plot to them. If you drop from Integrity 7 to 3 in the first two sessions; then there's no time to roleplay your decline.<br /> <br /> More importantly. Hunter has multiple sources of psychological horror: There's the isolation from friends and family. There's the horror of choosing between protecting your kids from monsters or putting food on their plate. There's the horror of the unknown. And of course, there's the horror of being a killer.<br /> <br /> As a toolbox game, it should provide tools to let me create a story, or even a charachter, that focuses on one particular source of horror above the others. If I want to create a charachter / story that draws psychological horror from the growing rifts between my charachter and her family I should be able to downplay the psychological importance of killing monsters and play up the importance of friends and family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808119#post808119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More reasons I prefer specific types of creatures as exemptions from the Code, rather than monsters in general. The moral ambiguity is what makes it interesting. Who is it or isn't it ok to kill, and what are the moral implications of the lines a character chooses to draw?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. I think that there are better ways than Breaking Points to show this though. It's the arguments with other charachters and<br /> <br /> Ooooh! I just had an idea! I think you're going to love this.<br /> <br /> What if The Code can't say &quot;X isn't a breaking point&quot;. It can only invert things so that &quot;Instead of X, not X is a breaking point&quot;.<br /> <br /> So for example. You can't have a Code that says &quot;killing a vampire is ok&quot; but you can have a Code that says &quot;killing a vampire is ok; sparing a vampire's life is a Breaking Point&quot;.<br /> <br /> This has three advantages.<br /> <br /> 1) It has an automatic balance. A code &quot;Suffer not a witch to live&quot; has both advantages and disadvantages over &quot;suffer not a supernatual to live&quot;<br /> 2) It has a very very natural path to being a Slasher. The moment your code says you must kill regular mortals (no matter how rare the circumstances) you're in the danger zone.<br /> 3) Possibly the biggest one: You automatically create mechanical space for drama centred around that kind of ambiguity. The MM hunter with &quot;Suffer not a witch to live&quot; has a breaking point when he wants to show mercy to a witch. That's probably the most interesting and dramatic time for one that's possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T12:59:25-08:00","id":808153,"title":"","content":"The original rules for the Code involved swapping out one Breaking Point for another, as well as picking up a psychological quirk. I avoided suggesting that because so many Breaking Points in 2e are potentially fluid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:01:26-08:00","id":808155,"title":"","content":"They did, but there was no requirement for the new Breaking Point to be directly related to the old one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:02:19-08:00","id":808156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808144#post808144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually agree with the principal. However I don't think it would weaken the focus on horror to allow Codes which permit all monsters. In fact, I think it would strengthen the personal horror. Hear me out on this one.<br /> <br /> I think that in most games of hunter (not Network Zero, but definately VALKYRIE) you're supposed to kill monsters regularly. I think that in practice a Breaking Point every time you kill a monster will numb the players and the plot to them. If you drop from Integrity 7 to 3 in the first two sessions; then there's no time to roleplay your decline.<br /> <br /> More importantly. Hunter has multiple sources of psychological horror: There's the isolation from friends and family. There's the horror of choosing between protecting your kids from monsters or putting food on their plate. There's the horror of the unknown. And of course, there's the horror of being a killer.<br /> <br /> As a toolbox game, it should provide tools to let me create a story, or even a charachter, that focuses on one particular source of horror above the others. If I want to create a charachter / story that draws psychological horror from the growing rifts between my charachter and her family I should be able to downplay the psychological importance of killing monsters and play up the importance of friends and family.<br /> <br /> Sure. I think that there are better ways than Breaking Points to show this though. It's the arguments with other charachters and<br /> <br /> Ooooh! I just had an idea! I think you're going to love this.<br /> <br /> What if The Code can't say &amp;quot;X isn't a breaking point&amp;quot;. It can only invert things so that &amp;quot;Instead of X, not X is a breaking point&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> So for example. You can't have a Code that says &amp;quot;killing a vampire is ok&amp;quot; but you can have a Code that says &amp;quot;killing a vampire is ok; sparing a vampire's life is a Breaking Point&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> This has three advantages.<br /> <br /> 1) It has an automatic balance. A code &amp;quot;Suffer not a witch to live&amp;quot; has both advantages and disadvantages over &amp;quot;suffer not a supernatual to live&amp;quot;<br /> 2) It has a very very natural path to being a Slasher. The moment your code says you must kill regular mortals (no matter how rare the circumstances) you're in the danger zone.<br /> 3) Possibly the biggest one: You automatically create mechanical space for drama centred around that kind of ambiguity. The MM hunter with &amp;quot;Suffer not a witch to live&amp;quot; has a breaking point when he wants to show mercy to a witch. That's probably the most interesting and dramatic time for one that's possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think that the Code should saddle you with some other disadvantage in exchange for removing a Breaking Point. Other Breaking Points is one way to do it. I think I prefer Dataweaver's suggestion of gaining Tells when you eliminate Breaking Points. Kind of like Banes in Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:04:28-08:00","id":808157,"title":"","content":"Oh. I meant in addition to Tells.<br /> <br /> My bad, I should have said so. That's how it worked in 1E so I assumed it would be obvious. In retrospect that was a silly assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:09:01-08:00","id":808158,"title":"","content":"Oh, gotcha. Yeah, I could see swapping one Breaking Point for another, in addition to gaining Tells when you do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:12:36-08:00","id":808164,"title":"","content":"With that in mind, do you like the concept of the new breaking point saying you have to do what the old one forbade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:14:28-08:00","id":808167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808164#post808164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, do you like the concept of the new breaking point saying you have to do what the old one forbade?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it at least being connected to the Breaking Point you got rid of, certainly. Maybe not necessarily always the opposite, but there should be a clear connection.<br /> <br /> Oh, on the subject of Hunters rapidly losing Integrity, that's going to happen whether or not killing non-humans is a Breaking Point, because &quot;witnessing the supernatural&quot; is also a Breaking Point, and that's kind of a Hunter's whole schtick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:17:13-08:00","id":808170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808167#post808167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, on the subject of Hunters rapidly losing Integrity, that's going to happen whether or not killing non-humans is a Breaking Point, because &quot;witnessing the supernatural&quot; is also a Breaking Point, and that's kind of a Hunter's whole schtick.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definately gong to have to change. Perhaps immunity to that will be part of the Hunter template.<br /> <br /> IMO if Breaking Points are that common, they loose all ability to create drama or story. It would be like making feeding a Humanity 1 sin for Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-13-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:32:07-08:00","id":808184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808170#post808170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definately gong to have to change. Perhaps immunity to that will be part of the Hunter template.<br /> <br /> IMO if Breaking Points are that common, they loose all ability to create drama or story. It would be like making feeding a Humanity 1 sin for Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I've GMed over 40 sessions of Hunter with Integrity rules, and &quot;witnessing the supernatural&quot; had to go. It was tiring, undramatic and mechanically unsatisfying when one of the characters dropped from Integrity 7 to 3 in four sessions merely from seeing supernatural phenomena, and others had similar results. On the other hand, one character had good Resolve+Composure along with Meditative Mind 3 from the start, and lost maybe 3 points of Integrity over 11 months.<br /> <br /> And yes, the campaign was monster-of-the-week sandbox, and so I gave bonuses to rolls from killing as the monster hunting was the point of campaign. Greatest horror was gained from fucked up decisions characters did that had nothing to do with violence and spiral of despair some characters faced, not from endlessly wondering if it was wrong to dust murderous vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:32:20-08:00","id":808185,"title":"","content":"I mean, they kind of need to be frequent to matter. It's really pretty hard to fail Breaking Point rolls, unless they have really heavy penalties.<br /> <br /> And again, there's always The Code to get rid of inconvenient Breaking Points... At a cost. There's a good reason ordinary people avoid and even willfully ignore the supernatural in the world of Chronicles of Darkness. If you're going to confront it anyway, you're going to have to deal with the consequences. For some Hunters, that will mean developing severe PTSD as they slowly succumb to Integrity loss and Condition pileup, while for others that will mean using the Code to desensitize themselves to the trauma of the supernatural, with all of the issues that come along with desensitization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:45:30-08:00","id":808201,"title":"","content":"Better rare Breaking Points then boring Breaking Points IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:48:26-08:00","id":808205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808167#post808167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, on the subject of Hunters rapidly losing Integrity, that's going to happen whether or not killing non-humans is a Breaking Point, because &quot;witnessing the supernatural&quot; is also a Breaking Point, and that's kind of a Hunter's whole schtick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will only mention idea of one of users from other topic...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpanishInquisition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807844-hunter-2e-open-dev-follow-up-hunters-and-slashers?p=807961#post807961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I completely agree with this. In fact in my own GMC / Mortal Remains Hunter the Vigil game I've replaced the question, &quot;What have you forgotten?&quot; with &quot;What can't you forget?&quot; Which served to give players a definite motivation to hunt and me ideas about what sort of monsters they want to see. For example one PC survived a Slasher attack, when the Cell encountered a Slasher it put his character in the spotlight. Hunters are human - they're just incredibly committed they can't turn back.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>And yes, Breaking Points on witnessing supernatural should be limited - I proposed in our RPG club game that till the creation of Code character need to have BP from seeing <i>all</i> supernatural - after the Code, only most mind breaking. Then I would only point this in extreme situations - like, I don't know, someone turning on the left side from the inside or something like this ( think John's Carpeneter <i>Thing</i> here situations ).<br /> <br /> Interesting would be if Hunters should be immune on Lunacy or Sleeping Cure based on resistance to Breaking Points from witnessing supernatural. But this is probably an offtopic now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-13-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:11:55-08:00","id":808353,"title":"","content":"I haven't mentioned breaking points for supernatural witnesses because this thread is about hunters vs slashers. But yes, there's a problem there that needs to be addressed. Maybe start another thread for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T20:34:25-08:00","id":808424,"title":"","content":"I'm writing a note here because I want to come back to this thread and the companion thread when I have more time and my brain isn't fried. Short version, though, is that for me is that Hunters and -most- Slashers are very intrinsically close: while the supernatural is a crucible in which a Hunter is tempered and forged (and yes, I believe a hunter is significantly different from a blue-book mortal), a Slasher is so thoroughly warped and twisted by the factors around him that he comes out just as honed and dangerous, except for different prey, and I do very much like that Hunters that go wayward can end up as Slashers.<br /> <br /> I would also like to suggest that there -is-, in fact, room for Slashers-as-monsters - as either yet another possible stage that most Slashers never achieve, or as a weird byproduct of a supernatural force shucking someone's humanity from them so violently that they can't help but be metaphysically warped, the Slasher-as-monster allows STs to create easy DIY antagonists with supernatural abilties as well as serving as a place for all those supernatural or nigh-supernatural abilities some slashers seem to have instead of trying to fit those in as quasi-Endowments or whatever.<br /> <br /> Or, put another way: Norman Bates and Hannibal Lecter: serial killers. Jigsaw and Michael Myers: Slashers. Freddy and Jason: straight up monsters complete with dread powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:59:20-08:00","id":808507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/807377-open-dev-three-slash-slash-slashers?p=808119#post808119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that no matter how much Hunters tell themselves &quot;monsters don't count&quot;, monsters totally still count.<br /> ...<br /> More reasons I prefer specific types of creatures as exemptions from the Code, rather than monsters in general. The moral ambiguity is what makes it interesting. Who is it or isn't it ok to kill, and what are the moral implications of the lines a character chooses to draw?</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate a point I made earlier, this is why I don't think hunter-to-slasher should be emphasised. A hunter going off the rails is more likely to become ever more obsessed with monsters, finding them, killing them, seeing them everywhere: that's both realistic and in keeping with this dilemma. Their killing of humans derives from this point: a disregard for collateral damage, a stern attitude to people who work with monsters even under duress, and mistaking humans for monsters; but the <i>point</i> is still killing monsters. For slashers the point is killing humans. Even the existence of a prominent hunter goes bad and becomes slasher vector implies that those who are still killing monsters are ok, and pushes the question of whether monsters &quot;count&quot; off the table.<br /> <br /> ETA: Incidentally, since Buffy has come up, she established her track record very early as only going after monsters that are actively engaging in evil; the difference with vampires in that mythos is that that was biologically guaranteed to be true,<br /> <br /> ETA again: Short version of my previous argument would be that I think the vector of a hunter gone bad should resemble one of Beast's Heroes more than a slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 01-14-2016, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}